# Patch files must reach the working tree byte-exact: two of the quickjs
# patches are git binary deltas ("GIT binary patch"), which core.autocrlf=true
# (the Git for Windows default) corrupts at checkout — git apply then fails
# with "git diff header lacks filename information". Text patches also only
# apply cleanly against the LF submodule trees when kept LF themselves.
*.patch -text
# Shell scripts break under bash if CRLF-converted.
*.sh text eol=lf
